"note":"Russian words for the block palette, the page, the examples and what exported programs print. Blockly's own blocks and menus come from its msg/ru.js. Blocks use the infinitive, as Scratch does in Russian (запустить, ждать, сказать); instructions to the reader use the polite вы imperative. Counts are written as \"шагов: {n}\" so one form fits every number. Field names, status values, settings and product names stay in Latin letters, as do words like issue, pull request and runtime that Russian developers use as they are. Yes/no answers in exported programs take д/да and н/нет as well as y/n. Quotes are «ёлочки». In blocks, keys are block types and the English parts they replace; dropdown values never change, only their labels. In page, starters and python, keys are the English text, with {name} for the parts filled in. In examples, keys are the example keys. Page buttons named in block text use their Russian names (Запустить, Продолжить, Расписание, Программы). The words were made by a model and want reading by a Russian speaker.",
